[SPEAKER_00]: In regards to the sense of security and the sense of self, if you know what I mean, like that it's... it's like, you know, if something you thought was so solid and so secure, the first time you realize that actually it's just this flimsy house of cards, it's like a... Terrifying.

333
00:31:07,397 --> 00:31:07,997
[SPEAKER_00]: Terrifying.

334
00:31:08,157 --> 00:31:10,939
[SPEAKER_00]: But now, you know, if it's just a house of cards, it's a house of cards.

335
00:31:10,959 --> 00:31:12,400
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't expect it to be anything else.

336
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:13,741
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

337
00:31:13,861 --> 00:31:17,643
[SPEAKER_03]: If you, if you, through, again, through gradual training, sense of change, you actually stop fueling

338
00:31:18,395 --> 00:31:22,195
[SPEAKER_03]: Stop adding more fuel to the fire of passion, aversion and ownership.

339
00:31:22,879 --> 00:31:31,666
[SPEAKER_03]: Then, yeah, the more of the same recognition that this house of cards is flimsy and is going to collapse, the more you have it, the less unpleasant it will be.

340
00:31:32,207 --> 00:31:48,360
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it was unpleasant not because of the recognition, but because of your emotional involvement with the house of cards, dependence on it, views, refusal to allow it to be otherwise, out of that, again, gratuitous sense of ownership of the, you know, like the self-centered experience.

341
00:31:48,761 --> 00:31:49,101
[SPEAKER_03]: No, no, no.

342
00:31:49,121 --> 00:31:50,202
[SPEAKER_03]: But I want it like this.

343
00:31:51,465 --> 00:31:56,547
[SPEAKER_03]: The question is that even when the doubt cannot prevail the principle anymore, because it's part of it, it's within it.

344
00:31:57,708 --> 00:32:00,970
[SPEAKER_03]: That's how you go beyond doubt, by not having ability to doubt.

345
00:32:01,250 --> 00:32:02,030
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

346
00:32:02,390 --> 00:32:05,852
[SPEAKER_02]: The doubt doesn't hinder the basic insight anymore.

347
00:32:06,752 --> 00:32:07,893
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, yeah, exactly.

348
00:32:09,694 --> 00:32:18,178
[SPEAKER_00]: It's very bad to think that doubt is a sort of bad quality or

349
00:32:19,924 --> 00:32:21,044
[SPEAKER_00]: It's unpleasant.

350
00:32:21,084 --> 00:32:21,705
[SPEAKER_03]: It's unpleasant.

351
00:32:21,725 --> 00:32:25,266
[SPEAKER_03]: So, people naturally then, like, oh, I must, you know, I just can't bear this anymore.

352
00:32:25,326 --> 00:32:36,929
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it is a hindrance and from that point of view, it is a bad quality because it does require kind of inadvertently stepping back into that self-centered point of view.

353
00:32:37,329 --> 00:32:39,110
[SPEAKER_03]: That's only when the doubt is possible.

354
00:32:40,050 --> 00:32:46,412
[SPEAKER_03]: But if despite the doubt, in face of a doubting mind, you still see this, this is,

355
00:32:47,584 --> 00:32:55,906
[SPEAKER_03]: That, because it is such a fundamental principle, that if you develop it sufficiently enough, yeah, doubt is obviously second to it.

356
00:32:55,966 --> 00:32:58,547
[SPEAKER_03]: And you, even now, you can see how doubt would be second to it.

357
00:32:59,107 --> 00:33:04,848
[SPEAKER_03]: But the point is to keep having doubt included within the principle when doubt is there.

358
00:33:05,488 --> 00:33:08,309
[SPEAKER_03]: So, the question is not to how not to doubt.

359
00:33:08,509 --> 00:33:12,990
[SPEAKER_03]: The question is how to then surmount the doubt with the same principle of non-ownership.

360
00:33:14,199 --> 00:33:21,877
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, yeah, it just becomes impossible for doubt to access that which precedes it, which is a necessary basis.

361
00:33:25,175 --> 00:33:35,002
[SPEAKER_03]: Then, you might doubt other things, and then the doubt as a hindrance will still persist, in regard to this or that, in regard to pressuring the mind, trying to get you to act, to clarify, to fuel the craving further.

362
00:33:35,603 --> 00:33:36,884
[SPEAKER_03]: But it can never spill outside.

363
00:33:37,164 --> 00:33:44,630
[SPEAKER_03]: In the same sense, the conceit that's left, the sense of I am that's left, the degree of passion, aversion that's left, cannot spill outside into that...

364
00:33:45,390 --> 00:33:55,721
[SPEAKER_03]: Previously assumed attavāda and the the sense of self independent of these aggregates and this experience and everything else, the absolute master control that's outside of all of this, that's inconceivable.

365
00:33:56,542 --> 00:34:05,531
[SPEAKER_03]: You can have those thoughts as an empty phrases pretty much, but all you see is this, this, and that becomes meaningless thoughts, like shells of your previous beliefs.

366
00:34:07,891 --> 00:34:11,192
[SPEAKER_03]: And the only reason they were there is because you didn't know.

367
00:34:11,533 --> 00:34:12,253
[SPEAKER_03]: It was impossible.

368
00:34:13,213 --> 00:34:14,434
[SPEAKER_03]: You thought it was possible.

369
00:34:14,454 --> 00:34:19,936
[SPEAKER_03]: You assumed possibility of being outside of this experience as a whole.

370
00:34:20,857 --> 00:34:23,538
[SPEAKER_03]: Assuming the possibility of being outside of the five aggregates.

371
00:34:26,639 --> 00:34:35,563
[SPEAKER_03]: But when all you have is this body within this body, mind within the mind, or body within the earth, earth within the body, whichever way,

372
00:34:36,296 --> 00:34:43,982
[SPEAKER_03]: If when you have that simultaneous dependence that doesn't require you, that has no room for you, then there is no outside of that.

373
00:34:52,289 --> 00:34:52,949
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's good news.

374
00:34:53,089 --> 00:35:01,035
[SPEAKER_03]: Initially, same as you just said in terms of the house of God, having no outside will be scary, because you assume that's where the freedom is, but it's not.

375
00:35:01,636 --> 00:35:04,358
[SPEAKER_03]: If there were outside, that would be just another thing you're subjected to.

376
00:35:06,243 --> 00:35:07,864
[SPEAKER_03]: So, even worse thing we are subjected to.

377
00:35:08,064 --> 00:35:09,465
[SPEAKER_03]: Even bigger thing we are subjected to.

378
00:35:10,765 --> 00:35:13,407
[SPEAKER_03]: But all we are subjected to is this and this.

379
00:35:13,487 --> 00:35:14,207
[SPEAKER_03]: This, this is.

380
00:35:15,207 --> 00:35:15,688
[SPEAKER_03]: Which is all.

381
00:35:17,068 --> 00:35:22,911
[SPEAKER_03]: Which is the entire saṃsāra, if left unchecked and ignored.

382
00:35:26,473 --> 00:35:28,374
[SPEAKER_03]: But no, sometimes people can also think like...

383
00:35:29,515 --> 00:35:34,157
[SPEAKER_03]: Okay, maybe they don't take it on that level, but they think, oh, if I have the right view,

384
00:35:34,610 --> 00:35:36,411
[SPEAKER_03]: This doubt would not exist.

385
00:35:36,991 --> 00:35:39,912
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, doubting mind would not be able to be there.

386
00:35:40,132 --> 00:35:41,053
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, this is the other discussion.

387
00:35:41,073 --> 00:35:42,393
[SPEAKER_02]: It's actually the opposite, basically.

388
00:35:42,413 --> 00:35:42,693
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, yeah.

389
00:35:42,894 --> 00:35:45,174
[SPEAKER_03]: But it's like, no, no, no, you still are going to have a doubt.

390
00:35:45,535 --> 00:35:47,896
[SPEAKER_03]: But the facts are no longer for the sort of... Well, exactly.

391
00:35:47,916 --> 00:35:49,756
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's the other discussion we had a few weeks ago.

392
00:35:49,816 --> 00:35:50,517
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, yeah.

393
00:35:50,577 --> 00:35:55,219
[SPEAKER_03]: So, so, you know, it's just that the... How far can that doubt pervert the order?

394
00:35:55,799 --> 00:35:58,280
[SPEAKER_03]: That will not be... That, that will be reined in.

395
00:35:58,620 --> 00:35:59,200
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

396
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:00,801
[SPEAKER_03]: Because, again, your situation remains

397
00:36:03,561 --> 00:36:05,022
[SPEAKER_03]: You can have any hindrance.

398
00:36:05,062 --> 00:36:05,942
[SPEAKER_03]: With this, this is.

399
00:36:05,962 --> 00:36:07,183
[SPEAKER_03]: With this, sensuality is.

400
00:36:07,723 --> 00:36:08,964
[SPEAKER_03]: With this, ill-will is.

401
00:36:09,104 --> 00:36:11,505
[SPEAKER_02]: But you can't doubt that principle.

402
00:36:11,725 --> 00:36:15,107
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, yeah, you can say that, but you can still doubt whatever your doubt turns into.

403
00:36:15,127 --> 00:36:22,390
[SPEAKER_03]: It's just to recognize that while you're doubting it, there is a simultaneously enduring basis that's a necessary basis for that doubt.

404
00:36:23,251 --> 00:36:24,791
[SPEAKER_03]: So, that doubt is not yours.

405
00:36:24,951 --> 00:36:25,932
[SPEAKER_03]: There is no outside of it.

406
00:36:27,573 --> 00:36:30,234
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, so, because doubt is always about something.

407
00:36:30,612 --> 00:36:32,332
[SPEAKER_02]: There's something that you're doubting.

408
00:36:32,393 --> 00:36:32,633
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

409
00:36:32,793 --> 00:36:36,194
[SPEAKER_02]: You cannot just have the phenomena of doubt sitting there in the vacuum.

410
00:36:36,614 --> 00:36:38,514
[SPEAKER_02]: So, even from that point of view, it's intentional.

411
00:36:38,794 --> 00:36:41,175
[SPEAKER_02]: And as such, there has to be something that's doubted.

412
00:36:41,815 --> 00:36:42,135
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

413
00:36:42,155 --> 00:36:43,476
[SPEAKER_03]: So, unnecessary based on you.

414
00:36:43,496 --> 00:36:49,517
[SPEAKER_03]: But it's just that you put that craving and pressure of doubt first, and that which is doubted second.

415
00:36:50,718 --> 00:36:51,618
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, it's endless.

416
00:36:51,798 --> 00:36:53,739
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you can doubt the principle.

417
00:36:55,319 --> 00:36:56,059
[SPEAKER_03]: You can.

418
00:36:56,119 --> 00:36:58,200
[SPEAKER_03]: You can take it as an object and start doubting it.

419
00:36:58,260 --> 00:36:58,440
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

420
00:36:59,814 --> 00:37:09,758
[SPEAKER_03]: But that, of course, doesn't mean that, like, when you start doubting it, when you took it as an object, it ceases, basically, to be seen as the actual principle.

421
00:37:12,719 --> 00:37:17,081
[SPEAKER_02]: But then somebody who has the right view would know that that is not in accordance with the right view, I presume.

422
00:37:18,382 --> 00:37:18,602
[SPEAKER_02]: What?

423
00:37:19,042 --> 00:37:19,942
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, what you just said.

424
00:37:20,883 --> 00:37:22,724
[SPEAKER_02]: That the principle is just an idea.

425
00:37:23,444 --> 00:37:26,105
[SPEAKER_03]: Yes, but there's a difference between thinking about a principle

426
00:37:27,286 --> 00:37:31,727
[SPEAKER_03]: Strapulating it in an idea, which is very much something you can doubt, that's what the Buddha asked the monks.

427
00:37:31,767 --> 00:37:36,229
[SPEAKER_03]: Monks, the one who is not clear about this, that endures here and now, is he doubtful?

428
00:37:36,369 --> 00:37:36,589
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes.

429
00:37:37,369 --> 00:37:39,409
[SPEAKER_03]: The one who is clear, can he be doubtful?

430
00:37:39,489 --> 00:37:39,730
[SPEAKER_03]: No.

431
00:37:41,250 --> 00:37:41,830
[SPEAKER_03]: That's the point.

432
00:37:42,230 --> 00:37:52,013
[SPEAKER_03]: But yes, if you lose the clarity of this, this, on a present basis, and start thinking about it in terms of abstract thoughts, then, yeah, that's that's

433
00:37:54,755 --> 00:37:56,576
[SPEAKER_03]: It's the the ingredients of the principle.

434
00:37:56,936 --> 00:38:01,978
[SPEAKER_03]: The principle is only when your situation is the basis of it, when it's included, when it's felt, when it's there.

435
00:38:02,359 --> 00:38:02,679
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

436
00:38:03,179 --> 00:38:07,281
[SPEAKER_00]: And so that's a kind of a limit to how far then you could continue.

437
00:38:08,141 --> 00:38:19,686
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, yeah, if you have understood that principle and developed it to the extent necessary whereby you realize, oh, you know, my mind can turn to it, but it's ridiculous because I see that doubt within the principle.

438
00:38:19,867 --> 00:38:20,667
[SPEAKER_03]: Nothing can change.

439
00:38:21,147 --> 00:38:22,888
[SPEAKER_03]: Then, yeah, the mind will stop trying to doubt it.

440
00:38:23,696 --> 00:38:26,198
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, so that needs to be seen once only, I presume.

441
00:38:26,739 --> 00:38:27,719
[SPEAKER_03]: No, no.

442
00:38:27,739 --> 00:38:28,820
[SPEAKER_03]: Same, same.

443
00:38:28,860 --> 00:38:32,664
[SPEAKER_03]: There's going to be like polishing of the of the of the dirty brass pot.

444
00:38:33,804 --> 00:38:39,189
[SPEAKER_03]: And yeah, each time it's going to be cleaner, but only next time you'll see they can be even cleaner.

445
00:38:39,869 --> 00:38:46,215
[SPEAKER_01]: You described it, um, this week we were talking about as like a stretch every every time.

446
00:38:47,095 --> 00:38:50,098
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, yeah, yeah, like, like, if your mind sort of

447
00:38:50,809 --> 00:38:54,251
[SPEAKER_03]: falls onto the the senses or goes into the abstractions.

448
00:38:54,331 --> 00:38:57,172
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, it's almost like a like a mental stretch to hold on.

449
00:38:57,432 --> 00:39:05,956
[SPEAKER_03]: This situation is a whole, this body, element of earth within it, or whatever, this sense of self, on the base of this present enduring situation of the senses.

450
00:39:06,796 --> 00:39:07,997
[SPEAKER_03]: So, two simultaneous things.

451
00:39:09,077 --> 00:39:12,519
[SPEAKER_03]: And then you fall from it, sometimes just too doubtful to begin with.

452
00:39:12,879 --> 00:39:16,760
[SPEAKER_03]: That means maybe you're trying too forcefully to to set it up.

453
00:39:17,201 --> 00:39:20,362
[SPEAKER_03]: The point is to discern the principle on account of what's already enduring.

454
00:39:20,816 --> 00:39:25,739
[SPEAKER_03]: Not do it on account of, okay, now I shall see this, because that's always going to give rise to craving.

455
00:39:25,859 --> 00:39:26,239
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, yeah.

456
00:39:26,479 --> 00:39:30,082
[SPEAKER_03]: So, that's how we learn to think without craving as well, to intend without craving.

457
00:39:31,162 --> 00:39:35,305
[SPEAKER_03]: You intend on the basis of what's already there, semi-intended, so to speak.

458
00:39:35,885 --> 00:39:41,529
[SPEAKER_02]: So, to start with the situation as a whole, and within that, discern rightly, rather than starting with...

459
00:39:41,549 --> 00:39:43,730
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you start with situation as a whole, i.e.

460
00:39:43,770 --> 00:39:48,533
[SPEAKER_03]: with what you're attending, but within that, you don't attend the next thing, you discern

461
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:51,505
[SPEAKER_03]: The origin of that attention that's simultaneously present.

462
00:39:51,665 --> 00:39:54,571
[SPEAKER_03]: So, manasikāra and the yonis of it.

463
00:39:56,515 --> 00:39:57,818
[SPEAKER_03]: So, with this, this is.

464
00:39:57,858 --> 00:39:58,579
[SPEAKER_03]: That's what that means.

